Here are a few tips to help prepare your home for winter:

- Check and clean the chimneys of any fireplaces or wood-burning stoves;
- Inspect the insulation, making sure there are no gaps or cracks;
- Test all exterior faucets and plumbing, ensuring that they are properly sealed;
- Check the weather stripping around windows and doors and replace it if needed;
- Install storm windows and doors if needed;
- Schedule an inspection of the heating and ventilation systems;
- Test smoke detectors and fire alarms;
- Check the furnace and chimney for any damage or blockages;
- Add extra layers of insulation to attics, crawl spaces and walls;
- Clean the gutters and repair any issues with the roof; 
- Fill in cracks around the foundation to ensure that drafts do not enter your home.
